From: Reaper <JohnGrimmReaper@disroot.org>
Subject: [PATCH] DtSvc: make Saver.h self-contained

DtSaverGetWindows() exposes the X11 Boolean, Display, and Window types,
but Saver.h does not include a header defining those types.  Consumers
that include Dt/Saver.h directly therefore fail to compile unless an
unrelated X11 header happened to be included first.

Include X11/Intrinsic.h so the public header supplies the declarations
required by its own interface.

--- a/cde/include/Dt/Saver.h
+++ b/cde/include/Dt/Saver.h
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 #ifndef _dtsaver_h
 #define _dtsaver_h
 
+#include <X11/Intrinsic.h>
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 extern "C" {
 #endif
